### random_hex / random_salt expose failure instead of hiding it

#### random_salt returns 32 hex chars on a healthy host

- Verify: random_salt returns 32 hex chars on a healthy host
   - Expected: salt.len() equals `32`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: random_salt returns 32 hex chars on a healthy host")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val salt = random_salt() ?? ""
expect(salt.len()).to_equal(32)
```

</details>

#### random_salt output satisfies the entropy post-condition

- Verify: random_salt output satisfies the entropy post-condition
   - Expected: secure_entropy_hex_valid(salt) is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: random_salt output satisfies the entropy post-condition")
val salt = random_salt() ?? ""
expect(secure_entropy_hex_valid(salt)).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### random_hex never returns an empty string for a nonzero request

- Verify: random_hex never returns an empty string for a nonzero request
   - Expected: v == "" is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: random_hex never returns an empty string for a nonzero request")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
# Empty is now representable only as nil, never as a text value.
val v = random_hex(16)
expect(v == "").to_equal(false)
```

</details>

#### two successive salts differ

- Verify: two successive salts differ
   - Expected: a == b is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: two successive salts differ")
val a = random_salt() ?? "a"
val b = random_salt() ?? "b"
expect(a == b).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

